      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The superior ductility of FCC metals arises from multiple easily activated slip systems.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Copper is an FCC metal.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed starting material is pure, undistorted, and well annealed.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical tensile loading is applied under ambient conditions.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The FCC lattice has numerous {111} slip planes and high symmetry.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under stress, dislocation nucleation and propagation are important deformation mechanisms in copper.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8398136::chunk::001::introduction::d83bb5753a"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocations in FCC copper propagate easily along multiple slip systems.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Low stacking-fault energy and isotropic bonding in the FCC structure cause easy dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Easy dislocation motion produces greater plastic deformation before failure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8398136::chunk::001::introduction::d83bb5753a"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Copper will have greater strain to failure than BCC metals tested under the same conditions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8357793::chunk::001::introduction::0cf0f01e08"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "BCC metals generally have less favorable slip-system availability than FCC copper.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Some BCC refractory high-entropy alloys are brittle.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8357793::chunk::001::introduction::0cf0f01e08"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The expected ductility advantage is limited to ambient conditions, high-purity materials, and typical FCC microstructures without substantial processing defects.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The quantitative ductility enhancement can vary with composition, temperature, and microstructure.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
